/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/float.k-34-  // float % float (e.g. `number % 1.0` = the fractional part). OPAQUE for kprove, concrete for
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/float.k-35-  // krun. Python's float `%` is floor-based: a % b = a - floor(a/b)*b (K's %Float is IEEE
